Hello experts,

I have 8 computers connected to the sam KVM switch, all running the exact
same kernel 2.6.22.19-0.1 (that's suse 10.3).
6 machines have exactly the same hardware and the cursor follows the mouse
perfectly.
2 machines are different (1 asus board and 1 industrial pc) and there,
when I move the mouse, the cursor moves erratically and even acts as if I
had pressed buttons when I have not.  Cursor does not move if I do not move
the mouse.  Often the cursor seems to move in the same direction than the
mouse but with giant steps (about a quarter of the width of my screen).

The mouse connected to the KVM is an old PS2 three buttons (no wheel) mouse.
I have tried on the pc where I have problems
several linux command-line options such as
	psmouse.proto=bare,  psmouse.resetafter=1,
or xorg.conf options such as
	protocol="auto", protocol="ps/2" or baudrate="1200"
without result.

I also tried
	echo 1 > /sys/module/i8042/parameters/debug
but there's nothing I really understand in the debug output.

Is there any suggestion to what I can do to fix or help understand that
problem ?

Thnaks in advance

Philippe

